@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Creating Resources in Azure DevOps";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Learn how to create and manage resources in Azure DevOps efficiently.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Introduction -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">Overview</h2>
        <p>
            Azure DevOps provides a suite of services that help teams plan, develop, deliver, and monitor applications efficiently. 
            To streamline DevOps workflows, you can create and manage various resources such as projects, repositories, pipelines, 
            and service connections.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-devops-resources.jpg" alt="Azure DevOps Resources Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Managing resources in Azure DevOps enables seamless development and deployment.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Creating a Project -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Creating a New Project</h2>
        <p>To start using Azure DevOps, you need to create a project:</p>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Navigate to <a href="https://dev.azure.com" target="_blank">Azure DevOps Portal</a> and sign in.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click on <strong>New Project</strong>.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Enter a project name, description, and choose the visibility (Public or Private).</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Select the version control (Git or TFVC) and work item process (Agile, Scrum, Basic, or CMMI).</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click <strong>Create</strong> to initialize the project.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/create-project.jpg" alt="Creating a Project in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Setting up a project is the first step in Azure DevOps.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Creating a Repository -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Setting Up a Repository</h2>
        <p>Repositories are essential for source code management. To create a repository:</p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item">Go to your Azure DevOps project.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Navigate to <strong>Repos</strong> and click <strong>New Repository</strong>.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Choose a repository name, type (Git or TFVC), and default branch.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click <strong>Create</strong> to initialize the repository.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/create-repo.jpg" alt="Creating a Repository in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Repositories store and manage source code effectively.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Setting Up Pipelines -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Configuring CI/CD Pipelines</h2>
        <p>To automate builds and deployments, follow these steps:</p>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Navigate to <strong>Pipelines</strong> in your Azure DevOps project.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click <strong>New Pipeline</strong> and choose the repository source (Azure Repos, GitHub, Bitbucket, etc.).</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Select the pipeline configuration (YAML or Classic Editor).</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Define the build and deployment stages.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Save and run the pipeline.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/configure-pipeline.jpg" alt="Configuring Pipelines in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Pipelines automate build and deployment processes.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Best Practices for Managing Azure DevOps Resources</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Organize Projects Effectively:</strong> Use meaningful names and structure.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Branching Strategies:</strong> Implement GitFlow or feature branching.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Enable Security & Permissions:</strong> Restrict access based on roles.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Monitor Pipelines:</strong> Set up alerts and logging for failures.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Automate Deployments:</strong> Use Azure Pipelines for continuous integration and delivery.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/best-practices.jpg" alt="Azure DevOps Best Practices" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Following best practices ensures efficient DevOps workflows.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-dark">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Creating and managing resources in Azure DevOps is essential for modern software development. 
            By leveraging repositories, pipelines, and best practices, teams can enhance collaboration, 
            improve deployment efficiency, and streamline DevOps workflows.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/conclusion.jpg" alt="Azure DevOps Resource Management" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Efficient resource management in Azure DevOps accelerates development cycles.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>